            {
                "entry_id": "1899af90-75dd-3dad-9b7b-e7f80a8b088f",
                "word": "tog",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "a5d355d4-de31-4763-b3bf-628d58c2ea4a",
                        "entry_id": "1899af90-75dd-3dad-9b7b-e7f80a8b088f",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "togs"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "67c19cee-6762-36a0-8cc8-84d9d199bc32",
                        "entry_id": "1899af90-75dd-3dad-9b7b-e7f80a8b088f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A tautog, a large wrasse native to the eastern coast of North America."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "976754f7-01c5-40af-bbfe-ed28e47bc1d0",
                                "sense_id": "67c19cee-6762-36a0-8cc8-84d9d199bc32",
                                "text": "Though most jetty anglers fish the tip when looking for blackfish, tog can often be found along the entire structure."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f8767d7e-5736-4b32-b3c0-8077e207fab2",
                                "sense_id": "67c19cee-6762-36a0-8cc8-84d9d199bc32",
                                "text": "However, many locations hold plenty of keeper tog to 8 pounds, with several monster white chins over the 10-pound mark, particularly along the East End of the Sound."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "955a1b2c-615d-343d-9502-39674bee1e03",
                "word": "tog",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "eec2da97-2465-4b2e-b6f1-95cef9d8dde9",
                        "entry_id": "955a1b2c-615d-343d-9502-39674bee1e03",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "togs"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6513da2d-514e-3da8-a94a-ffd00bc8af19",
                        "entry_id": "955a1b2c-615d-343d-9502-39674bee1e03",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A photographer, especially a professional one."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "informal"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "eeee92a1-bc27-4315-8ce3-801c0724135f",
                                "sense_id": "6513da2d-514e-3da8-a94a-ffd00bc8af19",
                                "text": "Funny you should ask, I had a \"scene\" with a photographer, at yesterdays' Wedding, over the Groom's lapel Mic, the Groom was ok with it, but the tog, said it would spoil his photos, the Groom had a light jacket on, so it was visible, but, what else can you do?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "11ea11a2-efe7-4f54-961c-a470bce8254a",
                                "sense_id": "6513da2d-514e-3da8-a94a-ffd00bc8af19",
                                "text": "If the tog said he'd deliver A grade shots but actually delivered D grade – tog is at fault"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5f99c1eb-abb6-473d-9387-4cfe6f8b81b2",
                                "sense_id": "6513da2d-514e-3da8-a94a-ffd00bc8af19",
                                "text": "Been a tog for a few years now, bit by bit expanding my lens library and just the other day picked up a 16-35mm f4 IS, it's pretty great."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": [
